# Readability

Please prioritize readability over clever or complex solutions.

- Write the version a teammate can read without reconstructing a trick.
- Name the step. Prefer a small function, an early return, and a plain loop or `map` over nested ternaries, dense one-liners, and extra abstraction.
- Add a helper only when it removes real duplication or names something that is hard to see inline.
- Keep the public shape small. Do not add a pattern, generic, or layer for a single call site.

```typescript
// ❌ Hard to scan
const label = items.filter((i) => i.on).map((i) => i.name).sort().join(", ") || "—";

// ✅ Same result, readable
const activeNames = items
  .filter((item) => item.on)
  .map((item) => item.name)
  .sort();

const label = activeNames.length > 0 ? activeNames.join(", ") : "—";
```
